+-    "content": "# [Informational] Model Context Protocol (MCP) Tools Reference Manual\n\n## Overview\n\nThe \ud83d\udc4dkanban platform exposes 24 intent-driven Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools across three streamable HTTP surfaces (`2025-06-18` specification). Unlike conventional project management APIs that force agents to coordinate dozens of low-level CRUD endpoints, \ud83d\udc4dkanban tools encapsulate multi-step engineering workflows into atomic, type-safe operations.\n\nResponses are serialized using `InlineSafeDumper` compact YAML, stripping null values and empty collections to maximize LLM context efficiency and token economy.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Surfaces[\"Three Dedicated MCP Surfaces\"]\n        AgentSurf[\"/mcp/agent (9 Tools)<br/>Token budget: <= 1,850 tokens<br/>Target: Coding & QA Autonomous Agents\"]\n        DocsSurf[\"/mcp/docs (3 Tools)<br/>Token budget: <= 1,300 tokens<br/>Target: Documentation & Knowledge Bots\"]\n        AdminSurf[\"/mcp/admin (12 Tools)<br/>Token budget: <= 2,800 tokens<br/>Target: DevOps & Migration Administrators (AAL2)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph LOD[\"InlineSafeDumper YAML Engine\"]\n        Summary[\"lod='summary'<br/>Keys, titles, states only\"]\n        Standard[\"lod='standard'<br/>Balanced properties & assignees\"]\n        Full[\"lod='full'<br/>Exhaustive body, history & links\"]\n    end\n\n    Surfaces --> LOD\n```\n\n![MCP Access Studio and Scoped Token Governance](images/13-mcp-access-studio.png)\n\n![MCP Level of Detail Tiers Studio](images/21-mcp-lod-tiers-studio.png)\n\n---\n\n## Surface 1: `/mcp/agent` (Execution and QA Tools)\n\nDedicated to autonomous coding agents, test runners, and QA bots. Bounded strictly by caller permissions; contains zero administrative or destructive tools. CLI binary mental model: `kanban-cli-agent`.\n\n### 1. `search_tickets`\n- **Description:** Hybrid lexical and semantic search across project tickets with multi-attribute filtering.\n- **Required Parameters:** None.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `query` (string): Text or semantic query.\n  - `workspace` (string): Target workspace slug or UUID.\n  - `project` (string): Target project key (e.g. `KAN`).\n  - `states` (array of strings): Filter by state names (e.g. `['in_progress', 'todo']`).\n  - `assignees` (array of strings): Filter by username or agent handle.\n  - `cycle` (string): Sprint cycle slug or UUID.\n  - `modules` (array of strings): Filter by module slugs.\n  - `labels` (array of strings): Filter by label names.\n  - `blocked` (boolean): Filter for blocked or non-blocked items.\n  - `gate_status` (string): Filter by agent gate state (`pending_agent_gate`, `vetoed`, `approved`).\n  - `mode` (string): `lexical`, `semantic`, or `hybrid` (default).\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail: `summary`, `standard` (default), `full`.\n  - `limit` (integer): Maximum items to return (1 to 50, default 20).\n  - `cursor` (string): Pagination cursor.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent search_tickets --query=\"progressive error\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 2. `read_ticket`\n- **Description:** Retrieve complete ticket details, canonical Markdown description, activity feed, and access manifest.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Human ticket key (e.g. `KAN-42`) or UUID.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `workspace` (string): Workspace context.\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail: `summary`, `standard` (default), `full`.\n  - `comments_limit` (integer): Max recent comments to return (default 10).\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent read_ticket --identifier=KAN-19 --lod=standard`\n\n### 3. `create_ticket`\n- **Description:** Create ticket or atomic child tree (max 50 nodes, depth <=6; omit project and parent inside children).\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Target project key (e.g. `KAN`). Root only; inherited by children.\n  - `summary` (string): Single-line ticket title.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `description_markdown` (string): Canonical Markdown description.\n  - `state` (string): Initial state key.\n  - `priority` (string): `urgent`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `none`.\n  - `assignees` (array of strings): Handles of assignees.\n  - `labels` (array of strings): Label names.\n  - `cycle` (string): Cycle slug or UUID.\n  - `modules` (array of strings): Module slugs.\n  - `parent` (string): Parent issue identifier. Root only; omit in children.\n  - `start_date` (string): ISO 8601 start date.\n  - `due_date` (string): ISO 8601 due date.\n  - `children` (array of objects): Sub-issues to create atomically. Each child object requires `summary` and inherits `project` from the root and `parent` from its enclosing node; both `project` and `parent` must be omitted inside `children`. Max 49 items per node, total nodes <= 50, maximum depth <= 6.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent create_ticket --project=KAN --summary=\"Self-correcting error UX\"`\n\n### 4. `update_ticket`\n- **Description:** Update ticket properties, state, assignees, or Markdown body. State changes must use `transition_ticket`.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `if_match` (string): Concurrency lock (version hash) to prevent lost updates.\n  - `summary` (string): New title.\n  - `description_markdown` (string): Markdown content.\n  - `description_mode` (string): `replace` (default), `append`, `prepend`.\n  - `assignees_add` / `assignees_remove` (array of strings): Incremental assignee adjustments.\n  - `priority` (string): Updated priority.\n  - `start_date` / `due_date` (string): ISO 8601 dates.\n  - `cycle` (string): Move to cycle.\n  - `modules_add` / `modules_remove` (array of strings): Incremental module adjustments.\n  - `labels_add` / `labels_remove` (array of strings): Incremental label adjustments.\n  - `parent` (string): Update parent issue.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent update_ticket --identifier=KAN-19 --summary=\"Refined Error UX\"`\n\n### 5. `begin_work`\n- **Description:** Atomic workflow starter: assigns calling agent, transitions ticket to started state, binds active cycle, and posts plan comment.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `plan_markdown` (string): High-level technical execution plan.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent begin_work --identifier=KAN-19 --plan-markdown=\"1. Implement schema validation\"`\n\n### 6. `transition_ticket`\n- **Description:** Transition ticket between workflow states, executing synchronous validators and triggering async agent gates.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `to_state` (string): Target state name or slug.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `comment_markdown` (string): Accompanying transition comment.\n  - `verification_proof` (object): Verification artifacts or test results.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent transition_ticket --identifier=KAN-19 --to-state=\"Done\"`\n\n### 7. `complete_work`\n- **Description:** Atomic terminal QA gate: verifies child blocker resolution, records verification proof, transitions to completed, and posts summary comment.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `summary_markdown` (string): Final delivery report.\n  - `verification_proof` (object): Passive forensic proof packet (logs, test outputs, screenshots).\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `to_state` (string): Target terminal state (defaults to `done`).\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent complete_work --identifier=KAN-19 --summary-markdown=\"Work complete\"`\n\n### 8. `add_comment`\n- **Description:** Post a canonical Markdown comment or threaded reply to a ticket.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `body_markdown` (string): Comment content in canonical Markdown.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `reply_to` (string): Parent comment UUID for threaded replies.\n  - `ack_mentions` (boolean): Acknowledge mentioned user notifications.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent add_comment --identifier=KAN-19 --body-markdown=\"PR review complete\"`\n\n### 9. `link_objects`\n- **Description:** Create or remove a typed Universal Object Graph link between two entities.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `source` (string): Source object key or UUID.\n  - `target` (string): Target object key or UUID.\n  - `link_type` (string): Relationship kind (`blocks`, `relates_to`, `duplicates`, `parent_of`).\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `create` (default) or `remove`.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent link_objects --source=KAN-19 --target=KAN-25 --link-type=\"relates_to\"`\n\n---\n\n## Surface 2: `/mcp/docs` (Consolidated 3-Tool Suite)\n\nDedicated to technical documentation, architecture specifications, and sticky notes. Consolidated from 6 legacy tools into 3 intent-driven operations (`search`, `create`, `update`). CLI binary mental model: `kanban-cli-docs`.\n\n### 1. `search`\n- **Description:** Unified discovery across Docs, Pages, and Stickies with hybrid lexical and semantic filtering, hierarchical breadcrumbs, and LOD tiers.\n- **Required Parameters:** None.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `query` (string): Search query text.\n  - `id` (string): Direct document slug or UUID lookup.\n  - `project` (string): Project scope filter.\n  - `type` (string): Entity kind filter (`DOC`, `STICKY`, `ALL`). Default: `ALL`.\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail: `summary`, `standard` (default), `full`.\n  - `include_tree` (boolean): Include full ltree hierarchical descendants. Default: `false`.\n  - `limit` (integer): Maximum items to return (1 to 100, default 20).\n  - `cursor` (string): Pagination cursor.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-docs search --query=\"architecture\" --type=DOC`\n\n### 2. `create`\n- **Description:** Atomic authoring tool creating standalone Docs, nested child Pages in an ltree hierarchy, or ideation Stickies.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `type` (string): Entity kind: `DOC` or `STICKY`.\n  - `title` (string): Document title or sticky summary.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project identifier (e.g. `KAN`). Required when creating stickies.\n  - `content` (string): Canonical Markdown content body.\n  - `parent` (string): Parent Doc UUID or canonical slug for nested document placement.\n  - `color` (string): Sticky color badge (`amber`, `emerald`, `sky`, `rose`, `violet`, `slate`). Default: `amber`.\n  - `links` (array of objects): Explicit Universal Object Graph typed relationships.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-docs create --type=DOC --title=\"Architecture Guide\" --content=\"# Overview\"`\n\n### 3. `update`\n- **Description:** Unified mutation tool for updating Markdown content, properties, or executing surgical line-level diff-patching with ETag concurrency protection and smart sticky-to-doc promotion.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `id` (string): Doc slug, UUID, or sticky note identifier.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `type` (string): Entity kind: `DOC` or `STICKY`.\n  - `title` (string): New title.\n  - `content` (string): New complete Markdown body (replaces entire content).\n  - `original_text` (string): Target substring for surgical line-level diff-patching.\n  - `replacement_text` (string): Replacement substring for surgical diff-patching (requires `original_text`).\n  - `parent` (string): Target parent Doc UUID to re-parent in documentation tree.\n  - `color` (string): Updated sticky color.\n  - `if_match` (string): SHA-256 ETag version lock preventing lost updates.\n  - `links` (array of objects): Graph relationships to add or remove.\n- **CLI Examples:**\n  - Full body replacement: `kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --content=\"# Updated Architecture\"`\n  - Surgical diff-patching: `kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --original-text=\"old line\" --replacement-text=\"new line\"`\n  - ETag-protected update: `kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --if-match=\"c4ca4238a0b923820dcc509a6f75849b\" --content=\"new\"`\n\n---\n\n## Surface 3: `/mcp/admin` (Governance and Lifecycle Tools)\n\nPrivileged administrative surface. Every request requires AAL2 credentials. CLI binary mental model: `kanban-cli-admin`.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Admin as Admin Agent (AAL2)\n    participant MCP as /mcp/admin Surface\n    participant DB as PostgreSQL Engine\n\n    Note over Admin,MCP: Phase 1: Dry-Run Inspection\n    Admin->>MCP: Call purge_invalid_links(confirm=false)\n    MCP->>DB: Audit dangling links & compute blast radius\n    DB-->>MCP: 14 broken links identified\n    MCP-->>Admin: Return dry-run summary + ephemeral confirmation_token (valid 300s)\n\n    Note over Admin,MCP: Phase 2: Explicit Two-Stage Execution\n    Admin->>MCP: Call purge_invalid_links(confirm=true, confirmation_token=\"tok_...\")\n    MCP->>MCP: Verify AAL2 session & token validity\n    MCP->>DB: BEGIN TX & DELETE dangling links & record audit event\n    DB-->>MCP: 14 rows removed\n    MCP-->>Admin: Purge executed successfully (Ledger ID recorded)\n```\n\n### 1. `configure_workspace`\n- **Description:** Read or update workspace-level settings, themes, and default project templates.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `get` or `update`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `settings` (object): Key-value workspace configuration settings.\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin configure_workspace --action=\"get\"`\n\n### 2. `manage_auth_cards`\n- **Description:** Configure, reorder, test, or toggle Multi-Card authentication providers.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `get`, `create`, `update`, `reorder`, `test_handshake`, `delete`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `card` (string): Auth card UUID.\n  - `slug` (string): Unique identifier slug.\n  - `provider_kind` (string): `local`, `oidc`, `oauth2`, `ldaps`, `webauthn`, `totp`.\n  - `display_name` (string): Card label on login screen.\n  - `public_config` / `secret` (objects): Provider configuration and write-only credentials.\n  - `after` (string): Slug of card to place after when reordering.\n  - `confirm_slug` (string): Required confirmation slug on deletion.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_auth_cards --action=\"list\"`\n\n### 3. `manage_principals_and_groups`\n- **Description:** Provision users, service principals, and groups, and manage role bindings.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `get`, `create_user`, `create_agent`, `create_group`, `bind_role`, `unbind_role`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `principal` (string): User or agent UUID.\n  - `group` (string): Group UUID.\n  - `handle` (string): Unique username or agent handle.\n  - `role` (string): `owner`, `admin`, `member`, `guest`.\n  - `scope` (string): Workspace or project scope identifier.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_principals_and_groups --action=\"list\"`\n\n### 4. `manage_access_policies`\n- **Description:** Inspect and update fine-grained 8-bit capability bitmasks (`VIEW` [0x01], `COMMENT` [0x02], `EDIT` [0x04], `TRANSITION` [0x08], `LINK` [0x10], `SHARE` [0x20], `ADMIN` [0x40], `DELETE` [0x80], `ALL` [0xFF]) on Universal Object Graph entities.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `read_manifest`, `grant`, `revoke`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `object` (string): Object UUID.\n  - `principal` (string): Target user, group, or agent UUID.\n  - `effect` (string): `allow` or `deny`.\n  - `capabilities` (array of strings): Granular capability masks.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_access_policies --action=\"read_manifest\" --object=\"<uuid>\"`\n\n### 5. `architect_project`\n- **Description:** Provision, configure, or scaffold a project using structured blueprint templates.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `create`, `plan`, `apply`, `get`, `update`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project key (e.g. `KAN`).\n  - `blueprint` (object): Complete project schema, workflow states, and default views.\n  - `plan_sha256` (string): Cryptographic digest verification.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin architect_project --action=\"plan\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 6. `manage_cycles_and_modules`\n- **Description:** Manage sprint cycles, functional modules, and custom view configurations.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list_cycles`, `create_cycle`, `update_cycle`, `start_cycle`, `complete_cycle`, `rollover`, `list_modules`, `create_module`, `update_module`, `list_views`, `create_view`, `update_view`, `bind_project_repo`, `list_repo_bindings`, `refresh_repo_binding`, `unbind_project_repo`, `help`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Target project key.\n  - `cycle` / `module` / `view` (strings): Entity UUIDs.\n  - `name` (string): Display name.\n  - `start_date` / `end_date` (strings): Schedule range.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_cycles_and_modules --action=\"list_cycles\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 7. `manage_custom_fields_and_scripts`\n- **Description:** Define custom scripted fields and sandbox execution settings.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `create_field`, `update_field`, `test_execute`, `escalate_scope`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project key.\n  - `field` (string): Field UUID.\n  - `tier` (string): `tier_a_wasm` or `tier_b_jail`.\n  - `target_scope` (string): `project`, `workspace`, `server`.\n  - `justification` (string): Cryptographic justification for privilege escalation.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_custom_fields_and_scripts --action=\"list\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 8. `manage_workflow_interceptors`\n- **Description:** Configure pre-transition helper hooks (validators, mutators, async agent gates).\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `create_hook`, `update_hook`, `reorder_pipeline`, `dry_run`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project key.\n  - `from_state` / `to_state` (strings): State transition rule.\n  - `hook_kind` (string): `sync_validator`, `sync_mutator`, `async_agent_gate`.\n  - `ordered_hook_ids` (array of strings): Execution sequence.\n  - `sample_ticket` (object): Test ticket for zero-persistence dry-run.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_workflow_interceptors --action=\"list\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 9. `manage_ai_and_agent_runners`\n- **Description:** Register LLM provider endpoints, configure token caps, and define CLI pipe harnesses or mTLS runner pools.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list_providers`, `upsert_provider`, `set_token_cap`, `register_runner_pool`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `provider_kind` (string): `openai`, `gemini`, `ollama`, `cli_pipe`, `remote_runner`.\n  - `base_url` (string): Endpoint URL.\n  - `token_cap` (integer): Monthly or billing period token ceiling.\n  - `mcp_allowed_tools` (array of strings): Allowlist of tools permitted for this runner.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_ai_and_agent_runners --action=\"list_providers\"`\n\n### 10. `override_ticket_provenance`\n- **Description:** Privileged administrative tool to adjust ticket author, creation timestamp, or state during migration reconciliation.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `reassign_creator`, `reorder_history`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `issue` (string): Issue identifier.\n  - `new_creator` (string): New author principal UUID.\n  - `reason` (string): Mandatory audit explanation.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin override_ticket_provenance --action=\"reassign_creator\" --issue=KAN-1 --new-creator=\"<uuid>\" --reason=\"audit\"`\n\n### 11. `audit_and_purge_object_links`\n- **Description:** Execute the Invalid Object Link Auditor to detect and remediate orphaned or corrupt graph relationships.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `scan_dry_run`, `purge_invalid`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `reason_filter` (string): Filter by violation class (`orphaned_target`, `cross_tenant_leak`, etc.).\n  - `reason` (string): Mandatory audit ledger explanation for purge actions.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin audit_and_purge_object_links --action=\"scan_dry_run\"`\n\n### 12. `destructive_lifecycle` (Two-Stage Confirmation Safety)\n- **Description:** Administrative destruction tool for projects, workspaces, or entire datasets. Enforces a non-bypassable two-stage confirmation protocol.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `request_delete` (Stage 1) or `execute_delete` (Stage 2).\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `target_kind` (string): `project`, `workspace`, `all_tickets`.\n  - `target` (string): Slug or UUID of target entity.\n  - `mode` (string): `soft_archive` or `hard_purge`.\n  - `confirmation_token` (string): Short-lived cryptographic token issued in Stage 1.\n  - `confirm_phrase` (string): Verbatim confirmation string (e.g. `DELETE PROJECT KAN`).\n  - `reason` (string): Mandatory audit justification.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin destructive_lifecycle --action=\"request_delete\" --target-kind=\"project\" --target=KAN`\n\n---\n\n## Progressive-Disclosure Self-Correcting YAML Error UX\n\nAll \ud83d\udc4dkanban MCP tools implement progressive-disclosure, self-correcting error responses. When an AI agent submits an invalid parameter name, misses a required argument, uses an unrecognized enum option, or encounters a domain concurrency conflict, the server intercepts the error before execution and responds with structured, actionable guidance.\n\nThis prevents repetitive LLM retry loops, hallucination thrashing, and context bloat by immediately providing:\n1. Exact culprit parameter name (`field`)\n2. Comprehensive list of allowed values (`valid_options`)\n3. Fuzzy and semantic closest matches (`did_you_mean`)\n4. Human-readable remediation instruction (`fix_hint`)\n5. Corrected, copy-paste-ready command invocation (`cli_example`)\n6. Line-numbered snippet candidates for ambiguous diffs (`closest_match`)\n\n### Pre-Dispatch Schema Validation Contract\n\nPre-dispatch validation runs centrally inside `McpProtocolHandler._handle_tools_call` across all 3 surfaces before tool handlers execute:\n\n- **Unknown Parameter:** The server checks common developer synonyms via `SEMANTIC_ALIASES` (`body` -> `content`/`description_markdown`, `identifier` -> `id`, `kind` -> `type`, `ticket_id` -> `identifier`, `title` -> `summary`, `originalText` -> `original_text`, `replacementText` -> `replacement_text`), camelCase to snake_case conversions, and `difflib` string similarity against known schema properties.\n- **Missing Required Parameter:** The server constructs a pre-filled `cli_example` containing all valid arguments the caller already provided, adding `<placeholder>` values only for missing required fields.\n- **Invalid Enum / Type / Pattern:** The server validates options against declared enum sets, computes case-insensitive closest matches (`\"dco\"` -> `DOC`), and returns typed format patterns (such as 64-character SHA-256 hashes).\n- **JIT Help Immunity:** Calls containing `action=\"help\"` or `identifier=\"help\"` bypass parameter validation to ensure help documents are always accessible without error.\n\n### Canonical YAML Error Examples\n\n#### 1. Unknown Parameter with Semantic Alias\nCaller passes `body` to `/mcp/docs` `update` instead of `content`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Unknown parameter 'body' for tool 'update'\n  field: body\n  valid_options: [id, type, title, content, parent, color, original_text, replacement_text, if_match, links]\n  did_you_mean: [content]\n  hint: Unknown parameter 'body'. Did you mean 'content'?\n  fix_hint: Unknown parameter 'body'. Did you mean 'content'?\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --content=\"new content\"\n```\n\n#### 2. Unknown Parameter with Fuzzy Match\nCaller has typo `querry` on `/mcp/docs` `search`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Unknown parameter 'querry' for tool 'search'\n  field: querry\n  valid_options: [id, query, type, project, lod, include_tree, limit, cursor]\n  did_you_mean: [query, cursor]\n  hint: Unknown parameter 'querry'. Did you mean 'query'?\n  fix_hint: Unknown parameter 'querry'. Did you mean 'query'?\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs search --query=\"architecture\"\n```\n\n#### 3. Missing Required Parameter with Pre-filled CLI Example\nCaller supplies `type` and `content` but omits required `title` on `/mcp/docs` `create`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Missing required parameter 'title' for tool 'create'\n  field: title\n  hint: 'Missing required parameter: ''title''. Provide a value to proceed.'\n  fix_hint: 'Missing required parameter: ''title''. Provide a value to proceed.'\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs create --type=DOC --content=\"# Architecture\" --title=\"<title>\"\n```\n\n#### 4. Invalid Enum Value with Case-Insensitive Fuzzy Match\nCaller passes `type=\"dco\"` on `/mcp/docs` `create`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Invalid value 'dco' for parameter 'type'; type must be 'DOC' or 'STICKY' or 'doc' or 'sticky'\n  field: type\n  valid_options: [DOC, STICKY, doc, sticky]\n  did_you_mean: [doc]\n  hint: 'Invalid value ''dco'' for parameter ''type''. Did you mean ''doc''? Valid options: [''DOC'', ''STICKY'', ''doc'', ''sticky'']'\n  fix_hint: 'Invalid value ''dco'' for parameter ''type''. Did you mean ''doc''? Valid options: [''DOC'', ''STICKY'', ''doc'', ''sticky'']'\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs create --type=\"doc\" --title=\"System Architecture\" --content=\"text\"\n```\n\n#### 5. Tool Not Found on Surface\nCaller invokes `search_docs` on `/mcp/docs` instead of consolidated `search`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: NOT_FOUND\n  message: Tool 'search_docs' not found on surface 'docs'\n  field: tool_name\n  valid_options: [search, create, update]\n  did_you_mean: [search]\n  hint: Verify tool name or switch to appropriate MCP surface endpoint\n  fix_hint: Tool 'search_docs' not found. Did you mean 'search'?\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs search\n```\n\n#### 6. Concurrency Conflict (ETag Mismatch)\nCaller attempts an update with an obsolete ETag version:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: CONFLICT_ETAG\n  message: concurrency conflict: ticket description was modified concurrently\n  hint: 'current etag: 9f83726abcde4582...'\n  fix_hint: Ticket description was modified concurrently. Retry with fresh ETag: 9f83726abcde4582...\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-agent update_ticket --identifier=\"KAN-19\" --if-match=\"9f83726abcde4582...\"\n  current_etag: 9f83726abcde4582...\n```\n\n#### 7. Sticky Already Promoted to Document\nCaller attempts to edit a sticky note that has already been converted into a formal Doc:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: ALREADY_PROMOTED\n  message: Sticky 'stk_01abc' has already been promoted to document 'DOC-KAN-42'\n  field: id\n  hint: Sticky 'stk_01abc' has already been promoted to Doc 'DOC-KAN-42'. Use update on that Doc instead.\n  fix_hint: Sticky 'stk_01abc' has already been promoted to Doc 'DOC-KAN-42'. Use update on that Doc instead.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"DOC-KAN-42\"\n  target_doc_key: DOC-KAN-42\n```\n\n#### 8. Surgical Diff Patch Target Not Found (Closest Match)\nCaller provides a target string with indentation or typo differences:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: PATCH_TARGET_NOT_FOUND\n  message: Target text not found in document\n  field: original_text\n  closest_match:\n    - line_start: 3\n      line_end: 3\n      similarity: 0.973\n      snippet: 'Section 1: Context'\n  hint: Verify exact whitespace and indentation, or inspect closest_match suggestions.\n  fix_hint: Target text not found in document. Inspect closest_match suggestions for exact whitespace/indentation.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"<id>\" --original-text=\"<snippet from closest_match>\" --replacement-text=\"<new>\"\n```\n\n#### 9. Surgical Diff Patch Target Ambiguous\nCaller provides non-unique target text that appears in multiple sections:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: PATCH_TARGET_AMBIGUOUS\n  message: Target text appears 2 times in document; provide more surrounding context\n  field: original_text\n  hint: Include unique surrounding lines to disambiguate the target region.\n  fix_hint: Target text appears 2 times at lines [1, 3]. Include unique surrounding lines in original_text to disambiguate.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"<id>\" --original-text=\"<unique context>\" --replacement-text=\"<new>\"\n  line_hints: [1, 3]\n  count: 2\n```\n\n#### 10. Entity Not Found\nCaller attempts to read or mutate a ticket or document that does not exist or is inaccessible:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: NOT_FOUND\n  message: ticket not found\n  field: identifier\n  hint: Ticket 'KAN-99999' was not found or you do not have access. Search accessible tickets first.\n  fix_hint: Ticket 'KAN-99999' was not found or you do not have access. Search accessible tickets first.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-agent search_tickets --query=\"KAN-99999\"\n```\n"
++    "content": "# [Informational] Model Context Protocol (MCP) Tools Reference Manual\n\n## Overview\n\nThe \ud83d\udc4dkanban platform exposes 25 intent-driven Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools across three streamable HTTP surfaces (`2025-06-18` specification). Unlike conventional project management APIs that force agents to coordinate dozens of low-level CRUD endpoints, \ud83d\udc4dkanban tools encapsulate multi-step engineering workflows into atomic, type-safe operations.\n\nResponses are serialized using `InlineSafeDumper` compact YAML, stripping null values and empty collections to maximize LLM context efficiency and token economy.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    subgraph Surfaces[\"Three Dedicated MCP Surfaces\"]\n        AgentSurf[\"/mcp/agent (10 Tools) - Token budget: <= 1,850 tokens - Target: Coding & QA Autonomous Agents\"]\n        DocsSurf[\"/mcp/docs (3 Tools) - Token budget: <= 1,300 tokens - Target: Documentation & Knowledge Bots\"]\n        AdminSurf[\"/mcp/admin (12 Tools) - Token budget: <= 2,800 tokens - Target: DevOps & Migration Administrators (AAL2)\"]\n    end\n\n    subgraph LOD[\"InlineSafeDumper YAML Engine\"]\n        Summary[\"lod='summary' - Keys, titles, states only\"]\n        Standard[\"lod='standard' - Balanced properties & assignees\"]\n        Full[\"lod='full' - Exhaustive body, history & links\"]\n    end\n\n    Surfaces --> LOD\n```\n\n![MCP Access Studio and Scoped Token Minting](images/slice3-mcp-access-studio-mint-modal.png)\n\n![MCP Config Snippet and Client Onboarding](images/slice3-mcp-config-snippet-modal.png)\n\n---\n\n## Surface 1: `/mcp/agent` (Execution and QA Tools)\n\nDedicated to autonomous coding agents, test runners, and QA bots. Bounded strictly by caller permissions; contains zero administrative or destructive tools. CLI binary mental model: `kanban-cli-agent`.\n\n### 1. `search_tickets`\n- **Description:** Hybrid lexical and semantic search across project tickets with multi-attribute filtering.\n- **Required Parameters:** None.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `query` (string): Text or semantic query.\n  - `workspace` (string): Target workspace slug or UUID.\n  - `project` (string): Target project key (e.g. `KAN`).\n  - `states` (array of strings): Filter by state names (e.g. `['in_progress', 'todo']`).\n  - `assignees` (array of strings): Filter by username or agent handle.\n  - `cycle` (string): Sprint cycle slug or UUID.\n  - `modules` (array of strings): Filter by module slugs.\n  - `labels` (array of strings): Filter by label names.\n  - `blocked` (boolean): Filter for blocked or non-blocked items.\n  - `gate_status` (string): Filter by agent gate state (`pending_agent_gate`, `vetoed`, `approved`).\n  - `mode` (string): `lexical`, `semantic`, or `hybrid` (default).\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail: `summary`, `standard` (default), `full`.\n  - `limit` (integer): Maximum items to return (1 to 50, default 20).\n  - `cursor` (string): Pagination cursor.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent search_tickets --query=\"progressive error\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 2. `read_ticket`\n- **Description:** Retrieve complete ticket details, canonical Markdown description, activity feed, and access manifest.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Human ticket key (e.g. `KAN-42`) or UUID.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `workspace` (string): Workspace context.\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail: `summary`, `standard` (default), `full`.\n  - `comments_limit` (integer): Max recent comments to return (default 10).\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent read_ticket --identifier=KAN-19 --lod=standard`\n\n### 3. `create_ticket`\n- **Description:** Create ticket or atomic child tree (max 50 nodes, depth <=6; omit project and parent inside children).\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Target project key (e.g. `KAN`). Root only; inherited by children.\n  - `summary` (string): Single-line ticket title.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `description_markdown` (string): Canonical Markdown description.\n  - `state` (string): Initial state key.\n  - `priority` (string): `urgent`, `high`, `medium`, `low`, `none`.\n  - `assignees` (array of strings): Handles of assignees.\n  - `labels` (array of strings): Label names.\n  - `cycle` (string): Cycle slug or UUID.\n  - `modules` (array of strings): Module slugs.\n  - `parent` (string): Parent issue identifier. Root only; omit in children.\n  - `start_date` (string): ISO 8601 start date.\n  - `due_date` (string): ISO 8601 due date.\n  - `children` (array of objects): Sub-issues to create atomically. Each child object requires `summary` and inherits `project` from the root and `parent` from its enclosing node; both `project` and `parent` must be omitted inside `children`. Max 49 items per node, total nodes <= 50, maximum depth <= 6.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent create_ticket --project=KAN --summary=\"Self-correcting error UX\"`\n\n### 4. `update_ticket`\n- **Description:** Update ticket properties, state, assignees, or Markdown body. State changes must use `transition_ticket`.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `if_match` (string): Concurrency lock (version hash) to prevent lost updates.\n  - `summary` (string): New title.\n  - `description_markdown` (string): Markdown content.\n  - `description_mode` (string): `replace` (default), `append`, `prepend`.\n  - `assignees_add` / `assignees_remove` (array of strings): Incremental assignee adjustments.\n  - `priority` (string): Updated priority.\n  - `start_date` / `due_date` (string): ISO 8601 dates.\n  - `cycle` (string): Move to cycle.\n  - `modules_add` / `modules_remove` (array of strings): Incremental module adjustments.\n  - `labels_add` / `labels_remove` (array of strings): Incremental label adjustments.\n  - `parent` (string): Update parent issue.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent update_ticket --identifier=KAN-19 --summary=\"Refined Error UX\"`\n\n### 5. `begin_work`\n- **Description:** Atomic workflow starter: assigns calling agent, transitions ticket to started state, binds active cycle, and posts plan comment.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `plan_markdown` (string): High-level technical execution plan.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent begin_work --identifier=KAN-19 --plan-markdown=\"1. Implement schema validation\"`\n\n### 6. `transition_ticket`\n- **Description:** Transition ticket between workflow states, executing synchronous validators and triggering async agent gates.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `to_state` (string): Target state name or slug.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `comment_markdown` (string): Accompanying transition comment.\n  - `verification_proof` (object): Verification artifacts or test results.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent transition_ticket --identifier=KAN-19 --to-state=\"Done\"`\n\n### 7. `complete_work`\n- **Description:** Atomic terminal QA gate: verifies child blocker resolution, records verification proof, transitions to completed, and posts summary comment.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `summary_markdown` (string): Final delivery report.\n  - `verification_proof` (object): Passive forensic proof packet (logs, test outputs, screenshots).\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `to_state` (string): Target terminal state (defaults to `done`).\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent complete_work --identifier=KAN-19 --summary-markdown=\"Work complete\"`\n\n### 8. `add_comment`\n- **Description:** Post a canonical Markdown comment or threaded reply to a ticket.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `body_markdown` (string): Comment content in canonical Markdown.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `reply_to` (string): Parent comment UUID for threaded replies.\n  - `ack_mentions` (boolean): Acknowledge mentioned user notifications.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent add_comment --identifier=KAN-19 --body-markdown=\"PR review complete\"`\n\n### 9. `link_objects`\n- **Description:** Create or remove a typed Universal Object Graph link between two entities.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `source` (string): Source object key or UUID.\n  - `target` (string): Target object key or UUID.\n  - `link_type` (string): Relationship kind (`blocks`, `relates_to`, `duplicates`, `parent_of`).\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `create` (default) or `remove`.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent link_objects --source=KAN-19 --target=KAN-25 --link-type=\"relates_to\"`\n\n### 10. `update_workpad`\n- **Description:** Update intermediate agent workpad notes, scratchpads, and execution progress on an active ticket.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `identifier` (string): Ticket key or UUID.\n  - `body_markdown` (string): Markdown content for the workpad.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `revision` (integer): Concurrency lock revision number.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-agent update_workpad --identifier=KAN-19 --body-markdown=\"### In-Flight Findings\\n- Root cause isolated\"`\n\n---\n\n## Surface 2: `/mcp/docs` (Consolidated 3-Tool Suite)\n\nDedicated to technical documentation, architecture specifications, and sticky notes. Consolidated from 6 legacy tools into 3 intent-driven operations (`search`, `create`, `update`). CLI binary mental model: `kanban-cli-docs`.\n\n### 1. `search`\n- **Description:** Unified discovery across Docs, Pages, and Stickies with hybrid lexical and semantic filtering, hierarchical breadcrumbs, and LOD tiers.\n- **Required Parameters:** None.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `query` (string): Search query text.\n  - `id` (string): Direct document slug or UUID lookup.\n  - `project` (string): Project scope filter.\n  - `type` (string): Entity kind filter (`DOC`, `STICKY`, `ALL`). Default: `ALL`.\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail: `summary`, `standard` (default), `full`.\n  - `include_tree` (boolean): Include full ltree hierarchical descendants. Default: `false`.\n  - `limit` (integer): Maximum items to return (1 to 100, default 20).\n  - `cursor` (string): Pagination cursor.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-docs search --query=\"architecture\" --type=DOC`\n\n### 2. `create`\n- **Description:** Atomic authoring tool creating standalone Docs, nested child Pages in an ltree hierarchy, or ideation Stickies.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `type` (string): Entity kind: `DOC` or `STICKY`.\n  - `title` (string): Document title or sticky summary.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project identifier (e.g. `KAN`). Required when creating stickies.\n  - `content` (string): Canonical Markdown content body.\n  - `parent` (string): Parent Doc UUID or canonical slug for nested document placement.\n  - `color` (string): Sticky color badge (`amber`, `emerald`, `sky`, `rose`, `violet`, `slate`). Default: `amber`.\n  - `links` (array of objects): Explicit Universal Object Graph typed relationships.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-docs create --type=DOC --title=\"Architecture Guide\" --content=\"# Overview\"`\n\n### 3. `update`\n- **Description:** Unified mutation tool for updating Markdown content, properties, or executing surgical line-level diff-patching with ETag concurrency protection and smart sticky-to-doc promotion.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `id` (string): Doc slug, UUID, or sticky note identifier.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `type` (string): Entity kind: `DOC` or `STICKY`.\n  - `title` (string): New title.\n  - `content` (string): New complete Markdown body (replaces entire content).\n  - `original_text` (string): Target substring for surgical line-level diff-patching.\n  - `replacement_text` (string): Replacement substring for surgical diff-patching (requires `original_text`).\n  - `parent` (string): Target parent Doc UUID to re-parent in documentation tree.\n  - `color` (string): Updated sticky color.\n  - `if_match` (string): SHA-256 ETag version lock preventing lost updates.\n  - `links` (array of objects): Graph relationships to add or remove.\n- **CLI Examples:**\n  - Full body replacement: `kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --content=\"# Updated Architecture\"`\n  - Surgical diff-patching: `kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --original-text=\"old line\" --replacement-text=\"new line\"`\n  - ETag-protected update: `kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --if-match=\"c4ca4238a0b923820dcc509a6f75849b\" --content=\"new\"`\n\n---\n\n## Surface 3: `/mcp/admin` (Governance and Lifecycle Tools)\n\nPrivileged administrative surface. Every request requires AAL2 credentials. CLI binary mental model: `kanban-cli-admin`.\n\n```mermaid\nsequenceDiagram\n    autonumber\n    actor Admin as Admin Agent (AAL2)\n    participant MCP as /mcp/admin Surface\n    participant DB as PostgreSQL Engine\n\n    Note over Admin,MCP: Phase 1: Dry-Run Inspection\n    Admin->>MCP: Call audit_and_purge_object_links(action=\"audit\")\n    MCP->>DB: Audit dangling links & compute blast radius\n    DB-->>MCP: 14 broken links identified\n    MCP-->>Admin: Return dry-run summary + ephemeral confirmation_token (valid 300s)\n\n    Note over Admin,MCP: Phase 2: Explicit Two-Stage Execution\n    Admin->>MCP: Call audit_and_purge_object_links(action=\"purge\", confirmation_token=\"tok_...\")\n    MCP->>MCP: Verify AAL2 session & token validity\n    MCP->>DB: BEGIN TX & DELETE dangling links & record audit event\n    DB-->>MCP: 14 rows removed\n    MCP-->>Admin: Purge executed successfully (Ledger ID recorded)\n```\n\n### 1. `configure_workspace`\n- **Description:** Read or update workspace-level settings, themes, and default project templates.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `get` or `update`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `settings` (object): Key-value workspace configuration settings.\n  - `lod` (string): Level of detail.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin configure_workspace --action=\"get\"`\n\n### 2. `manage_auth_cards`\n- **Description:** Configure, reorder, test, or toggle Multi-Card authentication providers.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `get`, `create`, `update`, `reorder`, `test_handshake`, `delete`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `card` (string): Auth card UUID.\n  - `slug` (string): Unique identifier slug.\n  - `provider_kind` (string): `local`, `oidc`, `oauth2`, `ldaps`, `webauthn`, `totp`.\n  - `display_name` (string): Card label on login screen.\n  - `public_config` / `secret` (objects): Provider configuration and write-only credentials.\n  - `after` (string): Slug of card to place after when reordering.\n  - `confirm_slug` (string): Required confirmation slug on deletion.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_auth_cards --action=\"list\"`\n\n### 3. `manage_principals_and_groups`\n- **Description:** Provision users, service principals, and groups, and manage role bindings.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `get`, `create_user`, `create_agent`, `create_group`, `bind_role`, `unbind_role`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `principal` (string): User or agent UUID.\n  - `group` (string): Group UUID.\n  - `handle` (string): Unique username or agent handle.\n  - `role` (string): `owner`, `admin`, `member`, `guest`.\n  - `scope` (string): Workspace or project scope identifier.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_principals_and_groups --action=\"list\"`\n\n### 4. `manage_access_policies`\n- **Description:** Inspect and update fine-grained 8-bit capability bitmasks (`VIEW` [0x01], `COMMENT` [0x02], `EDIT` [0x04], `TRANSITION` [0x08], `LINK` [0x10], `SHARE` [0x20], `ADMIN` [0x40], `DELETE` [0x80], `ALL` [0xFF]) on Universal Object Graph entities.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `read_manifest`, `grant`, `revoke`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `object` (string): Object UUID.\n  - `principal` (string): Target user, group, or agent UUID.\n  - `effect` (string): `allow` or `deny`.\n  - `capabilities` (array of strings): Granular capability masks.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_access_policies --action=\"read_manifest\" --object=\"<uuid>\"`\n\n### 5. `architect_project`\n- **Description:** Provision, configure, or scaffold a project using structured blueprint templates.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `create`, `plan`, `apply`, `get`, `update`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project key (e.g. `KAN`).\n  - `blueprint` (object): Complete project schema, workflow states, and default views.\n  - `plan_sha256` (string): Cryptographic digest verification.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin architect_project --action=\"plan\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 6. `manage_cycles_and_modules`\n- **Description:** Manage sprint cycles, functional modules, and custom view configurations.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list_cycles`, `create_cycle`, `update_cycle`, `start_cycle`, `complete_cycle`, `rollover`, `list_modules`, `create_module`, `update_module`, `list_views`, `create_view`, `update_view`, `bind_project_repo`, `list_repo_bindings`, `refresh_repo_binding`, `unbind_project_repo`, `help`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Target project key.\n  - `cycle` / `module` / `view` (strings): Entity UUIDs.\n  - `name` (string): Display name.\n  - `start_date` / `end_date` (strings): Schedule range.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_cycles_and_modules --action=\"list_cycles\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 7. `manage_custom_fields_and_scripts`\n- **Description:** Define custom scripted fields and sandbox execution settings.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `create_field`, `update_field`, `test_execute`, `escalate_scope`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project key.\n  - `field` (string): Field UUID.\n  - `tier` (string): `tier_a_wasm` or `tier_b_jail`.\n  - `target_scope` (string): `project`, `workspace`, `server`.\n  - `justification` (string): Cryptographic justification for privilege escalation.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_custom_fields_and_scripts --action=\"list\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 8. `manage_workflow_interceptors`\n- **Description:** Configure pre-transition helper hooks (validators, mutators, async agent gates).\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list`, `create_hook`, `update_hook`, `reorder_pipeline`, `dry_run`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `project` (string): Project key.\n  - `from_state` / `to_state` (strings): State transition rule.\n  - `hook_kind` (string): `sync_validator`, `sync_mutator`, `async_agent_gate`.\n  - `ordered_hook_ids` (array of strings): Execution sequence.\n  - `sample_ticket` (object): Test ticket for zero-persistence dry-run.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_workflow_interceptors --action=\"list\" --project=KAN`\n\n### 9. `manage_ai_and_agent_runners`\n- **Description:** Register LLM provider endpoints, configure token caps, and define CLI pipe harnesses or mTLS runner pools.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `list_providers`, `upsert_provider`, `set_token_cap`, `register_runner_pool`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `provider_kind` (string): `openai`, `gemini`, `ollama`, `cli_pipe`, `remote_runner`.\n  - `base_url` (string): Endpoint URL.\n  - `token_cap` (integer): Monthly or billing period token ceiling.\n  - `mcp_allowed_tools` (array of strings): Allowlist of tools permitted for this runner.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin manage_ai_and_agent_runners --action=\"list_providers\"`\n\n### 10. `override_ticket_provenance`\n- **Description:** Privileged administrative tool to adjust ticket author, creation timestamp, or state during migration reconciliation.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `reassign_creator`, `reorder_history`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `issue` (string): Issue identifier.\n  - `new_creator` (string): New author principal UUID.\n  - `reason` (string): Mandatory audit explanation.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin override_ticket_provenance --action=\"reassign_creator\" --issue=KAN-1 --new-creator=\"<uuid>\" --reason=\"audit\"`\n\n### 11. `audit_and_purge_object_links`\n- **Description:** Execute the Invalid Object Link Auditor to detect and remediate orphaned or corrupt graph relationships.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `scan_dry_run`, `purge_invalid`.\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `reason_filter` (string): Filter by violation class (`orphaned_target`, `cross_tenant_leak`, etc.).\n  - `reason` (string): Mandatory audit ledger explanation for purge actions.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin audit_and_purge_object_links --action=\"scan_dry_run\"`\n\n### 12. `destructive_lifecycle` (Two-Stage Confirmation Safety)\n- **Description:** Administrative destruction tool for projects, workspaces, or entire datasets. Enforces a non-bypassable two-stage confirmation protocol.\n- **Required Parameters:**\n  - `action` (string): `request_delete` (Stage 1) or `execute_delete` (Stage 2).\n- **Optional Parameters:**\n  - `target_kind` (string): `project`, `workspace`, `all_tickets`.\n  - `target` (string): Slug or UUID of target entity.\n  - `mode` (string): `soft_archive` or `hard_purge`.\n  - `confirmation_token` (string): Short-lived cryptographic token issued in Stage 1.\n  - `confirm_phrase` (string): Verbatim confirmation string (e.g. `DELETE PROJECT KAN`).\n  - `reason` (string): Mandatory audit justification.\n- **CLI Example:** `kanban-cli-admin destructive_lifecycle --action=\"request_delete\" --target-kind=\"project\" --target=KAN`\n\n---\n\n## Progressive-Disclosure Self-Correcting YAML Error UX\n\nAll \ud83d\udc4dkanban MCP tools implement progressive-disclosure, self-correcting error responses. When an AI agent submits an invalid parameter name, misses a required argument, uses an unrecognized enum option, or encounters a domain concurrency conflict, the server intercepts the error before execution and responds with structured, actionable guidance.\n\nThis prevents repetitive LLM retry loops, hallucination thrashing, and context bloat by immediately providing:\n1. Exact culprit parameter name (`field`)\n2. Comprehensive list of allowed values (`valid_options`)\n3. Fuzzy and semantic closest matches (`did_you_mean`)\n4. Human-readable remediation instruction (`fix_hint`)\n5. Corrected, copy-paste-ready command invocation (`cli_example`)\n6. Line-numbered snippet candidates for ambiguous diffs (`closest_match`)\n\n### Pre-Dispatch Schema Validation Contract\n\nPre-dispatch validation runs centrally inside `McpProtocolHandler._handle_tools_call` across all 3 surfaces before tool handlers execute:\n\n- **Unknown Parameter:** The server checks common developer synonyms via `SEMANTIC_ALIASES` (`body` -> `content`/`description_markdown`, `identifier` -> `id`, `kind` -> `type`, `ticket_id` -> `identifier`, `title` -> `summary`, `originalText` -> `original_text`, `replacementText` -> `replacement_text`), camelCase to snake_case conversions, and `difflib` string similarity against known schema properties.\n- **Missing Required Parameter:** The server constructs a pre-filled `cli_example` containing all valid arguments the caller already provided, adding `<placeholder>` values only for missing required fields.\n- **Invalid Enum / Type / Pattern:** The server validates options against declared enum sets, computes case-insensitive closest matches (`\"dco\"` -> `DOC`), and returns typed format patterns (such as 64-character SHA-256 hashes).\n- **JIT Help Immunity:** Calls containing `action=\"help\"` or `identifier=\"help\"` bypass parameter validation to ensure help documents are always accessible without error.\n\n### Canonical YAML Error Examples\n\n#### 1. Unknown Parameter with Semantic Alias\nCaller passes `body` to `/mcp/docs` `update` instead of `content`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Unknown parameter 'body' for tool 'update'\n  field: body\n  valid_options: [id, type, title, content, parent, color, original_text, replacement_text, if_match, links]\n  did_you_mean: [content]\n  hint: Unknown parameter 'body'. Did you mean 'content'?\n  fix_hint: Unknown parameter 'body'. Did you mean 'content'?\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"docs/arch\" --type=DOC --content=\"new content\"\n```\n\n#### 2. Unknown Parameter with Fuzzy Match\nCaller has typo `querry` on `/mcp/docs` `search`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Unknown parameter 'querry' for tool 'search'\n  field: querry\n  valid_options: [id, query, type, project, lod, include_tree, limit, cursor]\n  did_you_mean: [query, cursor]\n  hint: Unknown parameter 'querry'. Did you mean 'query'?\n  fix_hint: Unknown parameter 'querry'. Did you mean 'query'?\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs search --query=\"architecture\"\n```\n\n#### 3. Missing Required Parameter with Pre-filled CLI Example\nCaller supplies `type` and `content` but omits required `title` on `/mcp/docs` `create`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Missing required parameter 'title' for tool 'create'\n  field: title\n  hint: 'Missing required parameter: ''title''. Provide a value to proceed.'\n  fix_hint: 'Missing required parameter: ''title''. Provide a value to proceed.'\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs create --type=DOC --content=\"# Architecture\" --title=\"<title>\"\n```\n\n#### 4. Invalid Enum Value with Case-Insensitive Fuzzy Match\nCaller passes `type=\"dco\"` on `/mcp/docs` `create`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: VALIDATION_FAILED\n  message: Invalid value 'dco' for parameter 'type'; type must be 'DOC' or 'STICKY' or 'doc' or 'sticky'\n  field: type\n  valid_options: [DOC, STICKY, doc, sticky]\n  did_you_mean: [doc]\n  hint: 'Invalid value ''dco'' for parameter ''type''. Did you mean ''doc''? Valid options: [''DOC'', ''STICKY'', ''doc'', ''sticky'']'\n  fix_hint: 'Invalid value ''dco'' for parameter ''type''. Did you mean ''doc''? Valid options: [''DOC'', ''STICKY'', ''doc'', ''sticky'']'\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs create --type=\"doc\" --title=\"System Architecture\" --content=\"text\"\n```\n\n#### 5. Tool Not Found on Surface\nCaller invokes `search_docs` on `/mcp/docs` instead of consolidated `search`:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: NOT_FOUND\n  message: Tool 'search_docs' not found on surface 'docs'\n  field: tool_name\n  valid_options: [search, create, update]\n  did_you_mean: [search]\n  hint: Verify tool name or switch to appropriate MCP surface endpoint\n  fix_hint: Tool 'search_docs' not found. Did you mean 'search'?\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs search\n```\n\n#### 6. Concurrency Conflict (ETag Mismatch)\nCaller attempts an update with an obsolete ETag version:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: CONFLICT_ETAG\n  message: concurrency conflict: ticket description was modified concurrently\n  hint: 'current etag: 9f83726abcde4582...'\n  fix_hint: Ticket description was modified concurrently. Retry with fresh ETag: 9f83726abcde4582...\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-agent update_ticket --identifier=\"KAN-19\" --if-match=\"9f83726abcde4582...\"\n  current_etag: 9f83726abcde4582...\n```\n\n#### 7. Sticky Already Promoted to Document\nCaller attempts to edit a sticky note that has already been converted into a formal Doc:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: ALREADY_PROMOTED\n  message: Sticky 'stk_01abc' has already been promoted to document 'DOC-KAN-42'\n  field: id\n  hint: Sticky 'stk_01abc' has already been promoted to Doc 'DOC-KAN-42'. Use update on that Doc instead.\n  fix_hint: Sticky 'stk_01abc' has already been promoted to Doc 'DOC-KAN-42'. Use update on that Doc instead.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"DOC-KAN-42\"\n  target_doc_key: DOC-KAN-42\n```\n\n#### 8. Surgical Diff Patch Target Not Found (Closest Match)\nCaller provides a target string with indentation or typo differences:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: PATCH_TARGET_NOT_FOUND\n  message: Target text not found in document\n  field: original_text\n  closest_match:\n    - line_start: 3\n      line_end: 3\n      similarity: 0.973\n      snippet: 'Section 1: Context'\n  hint: Verify exact whitespace and indentation, or inspect closest_match suggestions.\n  fix_hint: Target text not found in document. Inspect closest_match suggestions for exact whitespace/indentation.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"<id>\" --original-text=\"<snippet from closest_match>\" --replacement-text=\"<new>\"\n```\n\n#### 9. Surgical Diff Patch Target Ambiguous\nCaller provides non-unique target text that appears in multiple sections:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: PATCH_TARGET_AMBIGUOUS\n  message: Target text appears 2 times in document; provide more surrounding context\n  field: original_text\n  hint: Include unique surrounding lines to disambiguate the target region.\n  fix_hint: Target text appears 2 times at lines [1, 3]. Include unique surrounding lines in original_text to disambiguate.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-docs update --id=\"<id>\" --original-text=\"<unique context>\" --replacement-text=\"<new>\"\n  line_hints: [1, 3]\n  count: 2\n```\n\n#### 10. Entity Not Found\nCaller attempts to read or mutate a ticket or document that does not exist or is inaccessible:\n\n```yaml\nerror:\n  code: NOT_FOUND\n  message: ticket not found\n  field: identifier\n  hint: Ticket 'KAN-99999' was not found or you do not have access. Search accessible tickets first.\n  fix_hint: Ticket 'KAN-99999' was not found or you do not have access. Search accessible tickets first.\n  cli_example: kanban-cli-agent search_tickets --query=\"KAN-99999\"\n```\n"
